\f2\b 2. Sea Sickness Ocean rowing / rough-water boats:\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f8\b0 \cf0 Seasickness is clearly possible in ocean rowing or rough-water boating. In these cases, the boat and rower are continuously moved by waves, producing stronger pitch, roll, and heave. The user is no longer only moving through self-generated rowing action, but is also being passively moved by the water. This can create stronger sensory conflict and discomfort.This reminds us a lot to motion sickness a form of cyber Seasickness, in which artificial movement is triggering nausea.
